    "description": "Some wearables infer physiological arousal from pulse, HRV, movement or skin conductance.",
    "content": "## Understanding the topic\n\nSome wearables infer physiological arousal from pulse, HRV, movement or skin conductance. Heat, movement and illness also alter these signals. They do not read thoughts or directly measure cortisol. [1](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27680542/) [2](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30245619/) [3](https://www.nhs.uk/every-mind-matters/lifes-challenges/maintaining-healthy-relationships-and-mental-wellbeing/) [4](https://support.google.com/product-documentation/answer/14779613?hl=en)\n\n## What you can do\n\nNote what you were doing and how you felt when the score changed. A break, gentle breathing or a walk may help; judge comfort rather than trying to improve a number.\n\n## What the evidence cannot tell you\n\nDefinitions and score directions vary by brand. Do not translate a stress score into hormone levels or use it to diagnose an anxiety disorder.\n\n## When to seek advice\n\nSeek professional support when stress or anxiety persistently affects sleep, work or relationships.\n\n## Sources and what they support\n\n1. [Draghici & Taylor (2016) — The physiological basis and measurement of heart rate variability in humans](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27680542/) — Physiology review. Supports: Mechanisms and interpretation limits of HRV.\n\n2. [Zaccaro et al. (2018) — How Breath-Control Can Change Your Life: A Systematic Review on Psycho-Physiological Correlates of Slow Breathing](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30245619/) — Systematic review. Supports: Slow breathing, HRV and heterogeneous evidence.\n\n3. [NHS — Maintaining healthy relationships and mental wellbeing](https://www.nhs.uk/every-mind-matters/lifes-challenges/maintaining-healthy-relationships-and-mental-wellbeing/) — Public health guidance. Supports: Communication, boundaries and managing disagreements.\n\n4. [Google — Find out what data Fitbit collects for Fitbit account users](https://support.google.com/product-documentation/answer/14779613?hl=en) — Manufacturer documentation. Supports: Device-specific data types, EDA and stress scores.\n\n> Content and sources updated: 2026-10-26. Educational content; clinical sign-off has not been recorded.\n",
