    "description": "Pelvic-floor exercises should match symptoms and use the intended muscles.",
    "content": "## Understanding the topic\n\nPelvic-floor exercises should match symptoms and use the intended muscles. Bracing the abdomen, holding the breath or squeezing the buttocks is not a substitute. Painful, tense muscles may need relaxation before strengthening. [1](https://www.nth.nhs.uk/resources/pelvic-floor-exercises-for-men/) [2](https://www.royalberkshire.nhs.uk/media/avwg3hls/pelvic-floor-strengthening-and-relaxation-exercises-for-men_jun24.pdf)\n\n## What you can do\n\nStart comfortably, gently contract as if stopping wind, breathe normally and allow full release. Quality matters more than repetition count. Ask for an individualized plan for leakage or postoperative rehabilitation.\n\n## What the evidence cannot tell you\n\nThere is no universal hold-and-rest schedule. Avoid regularly stopping urine flow as exercise or pushing through pain.\n\n## When to seek advice\n\nStop and seek assessment for new or increasing pain, pelvic heaviness or difficulty urinating.\n\n## Sources and what they support\n\n1. [North Tees and Hartlepool NHS — Pelvic Floor Exercises for Men](https://www.nth.nhs.uk/resources/pelvic-floor-exercises-for-men/) — Physiotherapy patient guidance. Supports: Identifying, contracting and relaxing male pelvic floor muscles.\n\n2. [Royal Berkshire NHS (2024) — Pelvic floor strengthening and relaxation exercises for men](https://www.royalberkshire.nhs.uk/media/avwg3hls/pelvic-floor-strengthening-and-relaxation-exercises-for-men_jun24.pdf) — Physiotherapy patient guidance. Supports: Strengthening and relaxation; not a prescription to tighten for everyone.\n\n> Content and sources updated: 2026-10-26. Educational content; clinical sign-off has not been recorded.\n",
    "takeaway": "Start comfortably, gently contract as if stopping wind, breathe normally and allow full release. Quality matters more than repetition count. Ask for an individualized plan for leakage or postoperative rehabilitation.",
