    "title": "Sleep difficulties before your period",
    "description": "Sleep problems can occur with PMS, while pain, environment and stress also matter.",
    "content": "## Understanding the topic\n\nSleep problems can occur with PMS, while pain, environment and stress also matter. A skin-temperature chart cannot show that progesterone removed a specific amount of REM sleep. [1](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/pre-menstrual-syndrome/) [2](https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/health/sleep-deprivation/healthy-sleep-habits) [3](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34314344/)\n\n## What you can do\n\nTrack sleep and symptoms for at least two cycles. Keep a reasonably regular schedule, a comfortable room and an appropriate pain-care plan. Focus on daytime function if stage estimates increase anxiety.\n\n## What the evidence cannot tell you\n\nNo exact room temperature suits everyone or guarantees restored REM. Wearable sleep stages remain estimates.\n\n## When to seek advice\n\nPersistent insomnia, substantial pain or daytime sleepiness affecting safety warrant medical advice.\n\n## Sources and what they support\n\n1. [NHS — PMS (premenstrual syndrome)](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/pre-menstrual-syndrome/) — Public health guidance. Supports: PMS symptoms, symptom diaries and care options.\n\n2. [NHLBI — Healthy Sleep Habits](https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/health/sleep-deprivation/healthy-sleep-habits) — Public health guidance. Supports: Sleep habits and consistent schedules.\n\n3. [Schutte-Rodin et al. (2021) — Evaluating consumer and clinical sleep technologies: an American Academy of Sleep Medicine update](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34314344/) — Professional society review. Supports: Evaluation and validation limits of sleep technologies.\n\n> Content and sources updated: 2026-10-26. Educational content; clinical sign-off has not been recorded.\n",
    "takeaway": "Track sleep and symptoms for at least two cycles. Keep a reasonably regular schedule, a comfortable room and an appropriate pain-care plan. Focus on daytime function if stage estimates increase anxiety.",
