    "trigger": "User taps info icon (i) or 'Learn more' on the Menstrual Cycle & Pregnancy Tracking card",
    "title": "Early pregnancy signs and reliable testing",
    "description": "A missed period, breast tenderness, fatigue or nausea can occur in pregnancy but also have other causes.",
    "content": "## Understanding the topic\n\nA missed period, breast tenderness, fatigue or nausea can occur in pregnancy but also have other causes. Higher pulse or skin temperature cannot confirm pregnancy or show normal development. [1](https://www.nhs.uk/pregnancy/trying-for-a-baby/doing-a-pregnancy-test/) [2](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/ectopic-pregnancy/symptoms/)\n\n## What you can do\n\nTest from the first day of a missed period, or at least 21 days after the last unprotected sex if dates are unclear. Repeat after a few days if an early negative result does not resolve uncertainty.\n\n## What the evidence cannot tell you\n\nTemperature changes do not reliably identify implantation. Light bleeding cannot distinguish normal pregnancy, a period and a problem requiring assessment.\n\n## When to seek advice\n\nPossible pregnancy with one-sided pain, shoulder pain, faintness or bleeding needs urgent assessment even without a positive test.\n\n## Sources and what they support\n\n1. [NHS — Doing a pregnancy test](https://www.nhs.uk/pregnancy/trying-for-a-baby/doing-a-pregnancy-test/) — Public health guidance. Supports: Pregnancy test timing and early negative results.\n\n2. [NHS — Ectopic pregnancy: symptoms](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/ectopic-pregnancy/symptoms/) — Public health guidance. Supports: Pain, bleeding, shoulder pain and urgent care.\n\n> Content and sources updated: 2026-10-26. Educational content; clinical sign-off has not been recorded.\n",
    "takeaway": "Test from the first day of a missed period, or at least 21 days after the last unprotected sex if dates are unclear. Repeat after a few days if an early negative result does not resolve uncertainty.",
    "reading_time": "1 min",
    "thumbnail": "images/editorial/WH_24_hero.svg",
    "source_name": "NHS — Doing a pregnancy test",
