    "description": "Endometriosis can cause pelvic or period pain, pain during sex and fertility difficulties.",
    "content": "## Understanding the topic\n\nEndometriosis can cause pelvic or period pain, pain during sex and fertility difficulties. Pain severity does not simply measure disease extent. Symptoms can overlap other conditions and require assessment. [1](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/endometriosis/) [2](https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/when-sex-is-painful)\n\n## What you can do\n\nRecord timing, daily-life impact, bowel or bladder symptoms and measures already tried. Bring the record to assessment and discuss a treatment and follow-up plan if symptoms persist.\n\n## What the evidence cannot tell you\n\nAn initially normal assessment does not explain all pelvic pain. HRV and cycle apps cannot diagnose or exclude endometriosis.\n\n## When to seek advice\n\nPain affecting study, work, sex or fertility warrants assessment. Sudden severe pain needs urgent care.\n\n## Sources and what they support\n\n1. [NHS — Endometriosis](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/endometriosis/) — Public health guidance. Supports: Endometriosis symptoms, assessment and treatment.\n\n2. [ACOG — When Sex Is Painful](https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/when-sex-is-painful) — Professional patient guidance. Supports: Causes and care of painful sex.\n\n> Content and sources updated: 2026-10-26. Educational content; clinical sign-off has not been recorded.\n",
