    "description": "Changing periods, hot flushes, sleep difficulties and vaginal dryness can occur during the transition.",
    "content": "## Understanding the topic\n\nChanging periods, hot flushes, sleep difficulties and vaginal dryness can occur during the transition. Symptoms vary and may substantially affect quality of life. Not every midlife palpitation or fatigue symptom is menopause. [1](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/menopause-and-perimenopause/symptoms/) [2](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/menopause-and-perimenopause/treatment/) [3](https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/vulvovaginal-health)\n\n## What you can do\n\nRecord your main symptoms and care priorities. Support activity and nutrition and discuss hormonal and non-hormonal options with a clinician, considering history, benefits, risks and preferences.\n\n## What the evidence cannot tell you\n\nSkin temperature or one hormone result cannot automatically establish the stage. Herbal and hormone-balance products should not be assumed effective or safe.\n\n## When to seek advice\n\nPostmenopausal bleeding, marked bleeding changes or suspected early menopause warrant assessment.\n\n## Sources and what they support\n\n1. [NHS — Symptoms of menopause and perimenopause](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/menopause-and-perimenopause/symptoms/) — Public health guidance. Supports: Perimenopause and menopause symptoms; seeking care.\n\n2. [NHS — Menopause and perimenopause: treatment](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/menopause-and-perimenopause/treatment/) — Public health guidance. Supports: Discussing benefits and risks of menopause symptom treatment.\n\n3. [ACOG — Vulvovaginal Health](https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/vulvovaginal-health) — Professional patient guidance. Supports: Vulvovaginal care, discharge, tissue changes and treatments.\n\n> Content and sources updated: 2026-10-26. Educational content; clinical sign-off has not been recorded.\n",
    "takeaway": "Record your main symptoms and care priorities. Support activity and nutrition and discuss hormonal and non-hormonal options with a clinician, considering history, benefits, risks and preferences.",
    "reading_time": "1 min",
    "thumbnail": "images/editorial/WH_30_hero.svg",
    "source_name": "NHS — Symptoms of menopause and perimenopause",
    "source_url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/menopause-and-perimenopause/symptoms/",
    "hero_image": "images/editorial/WH_30_hero.svg",
