    "description": "Helpful communication involves expressing experiences, listening and respecting boundaries.",
    "content": "## Understanding the topic\n\nHelpful communication involves expressing experiences, listening and respecting boundaries. No positive-to-negative comment ratio guarantees a healthy relationship. Context and treatment of each other matter more than a score. [1](https://www.nhs.uk/every-mind-matters/lifes-challenges/maintaining-healthy-relationships-and-mental-wellbeing/) [2](https://www.devonsexualhealth.nhs.uk/your-sexual-health/relationships-and-intimacy/)\n\n## What you can do\n\nPractice suggestion: choose one issue, describe your experience and request, then check understanding. Take turns and agree one small action to try rather than resolving every disagreement at once.\n\n## What the evidence cannot tell you\n\nThis is a communication exercise, not a treatment formula or an oxytocin intervention. It should not be used to pressure agreement.\n\n## When to seek advice\n\nThreats, coercion or violence call for safety and individual support rather than communication tips alone.\n\n## Sources and what they support\n\n1. [NHS — Maintaining healthy relationships and mental wellbeing](https://www.nhs.uk/every-mind-matters/lifes-challenges/maintaining-healthy-relationships-and-mental-wellbeing/) — Public health guidance. Supports: Communication, boundaries and managing disagreements.\n\n2. [Devon Sexual Health (NHS) — Relationships and intimacy](https://www.devonsexualhealth.nhs.uk/your-sexual-health/relationships-and-intimacy/) — Sexual health service guidance. Supports: Consent, intimacy and masturbation.\n\n> Content and sources updated: 2026-10-26. Educational content; clinical sign-off has not been recorded.\n",
