    "description": "Fluid needs depend on weather, activity duration, sweating, food and health.",
    "content": "## Understanding the topic\n\nFluid needs depend on weather, activity duration, sweating, food and health. Thirst, less urine and dark urine can suggest dehydration, but color or pulse alone cannot quantify a fluid deficit. [1](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/dehydration/)\n\n## What you can do\n\nHave water available and adjust to thirst, conditions and individual advice. Long or hot sessions may need a tailored fluid and electrolyte plan. Do not force large volumes to meet an app target.\n\n## What the evidence cannot tell you\n\nNo single ml/kg formula or 2% loss threshold predicts everyone's performance. Prescribed fluid restrictions take priority.\n\n## When to seek advice\n\nPersistent dizziness, very little urine, confusion or breathing difficulty require medical care rather than continuing exercise and drinking.\n\n## Sources and what they support\n\n1. [NHS — Dehydration](https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/dehydration/) — Public health guidance. Supports: Dehydration symptoms and when urgent care is needed.\n\n> Content and sources updated: 2026-10-26. Educational content; clinical sign-off has not been recorded.\n",
